				{
					"id": "tA-smJrMuhZZXT4Pg",
					"name": "Gate of Infinity",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Tears a hole between two points in real space and steps through — the rarest and most feared telekinetic feat, since a botched Gate can open into the warp itself instead.\n\nDesign: Built on Basic's own Warp advantage (B99, instant travel to any place you have seen/visualized, flat 100), with Preparation Required (-20%, B113, a few seconds' concentration) and the Severe Perils tier, reflecting the setting's specific fear of a failed Gate opening into the immaterium. Net -60%. Full modified cost: 100 x 0.4 = 40 points — the single most expensive non-Great-Power ability in this file; needs Warp Empowerment level 3 (cap 40), the minimum at which \"Delta and up\" can cast the full non-Great-Power roster, exactly on the cap with no headroom to spare.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "mFOTAZTn1VLSKy6fh",
							"name": "Preparation Required",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mup-BAHqN509X3TVX",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mnuW03io683O_svNR",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Severe)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 100
				}
			]
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "s23deCcqQeSKMci99",
			"name": "Psyniscience",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The trained (or instinctive) sense of \"something wrong\" in a presence, place, or object touched by the warp — a chill in a corridor, a servitor's dead eyes going wrong. Named for the Dark Heresy/Only War skill of the same purpose (Psyniscience), used here for calibration only; the GURPS build is original.\n\nDesign: New skill per framework.md (\"New skills only when nothing fits\"). Per/H, Talent-affected: characters with a Psyker Talent (see the psyker power library — not part of this file) get it at a discount per that trait's rules and may default it from Per at a penalty; an unaugmented human without any psychic Talent cannot default into it at all (there is nothing latent to sense with) and must buy it as an unusual background purchase, if a GM allows it at all — most unaugmented Imperial citizens simply never take this skill.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Psionic"
			],
			"difficulty": "per/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sWDd1JQa3ebA4hKvJ",
			"name": "Meditation",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The discipline every Librarian drills to hold their gift steady under fire.\n\nDesign: Hard skill, a Librarian's IQ+0 or better; points left generic since this add-on does not know the base template's final IQ.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "s9nHN54DsHplKsDFq",
			"name": "Hidden Lore",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Librarian's formal training in the Chapter's Librarius doctrine on the immaterium.\n\nDesign: Average skill; points as above.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"specialization": "the Warp",
			"difficulty": "iq/a",
			"points": 4
		},
		{
			"id": "sV_jetDKpWXhdFBnr",
			"name": "Broadsword",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Many Librarians favour a force weapon over a chainsword once raised to the Librarius.\n\nDesign: Force swords use Broadsword (framework weapon-skill table), which the Battle-Brother template already has. These 4 points are added on top of it; merge the two Broadsword entries on the sheet.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 4
		}
	],
	"equipment": [
		{
			"id": "e1qCNzxXbhYpTQZxE",
			"description": "Force Sword",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A disruption-field blade further warded and psychically attuned so a trained mind can channel force directly through it — standard wargear for Inquisitors, Sisters of the Ordo Hereticus with psychic gifts, and any Astartes Librarian who favours a blade over a staff. Depicted throughout Black Library (Eisenhorn's own force sword; Grey Knights' force weapons) and Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader's force-weapon rules.\n\nDesign: Built directly on the framework's rescaled power-field rule: field off is the mundane fine blade (sw+1 cut), field on adds +3d and armour divisor (10) per the updated rule (\"Bladed/mace power weapons add +3d over the mundane weapon\"), landing exactly on the rescaled power sword anchor (sw+3d(10) cut) — a force sword is mechanically a power sword that a trained mind can also channel psychic force through. The Force Strike line shows that channelling: same dice as field-on minus the armour divisor, but its ignores-DR component only applies against Warp-touched targets, so it never trivialises ordinary armour. Its damage scales narratively with the wielder's Psyker Talent level (+1d per Psyker Talent level on top of the base 3d, GM's call above level 2) rather than as a fixed number, since the build tool's damage syntax cannot encode a variable.",
